(FIL-103: a `value` is refused as a `Write` source — its type is only
 known at runtime, so the compiler cannot tell a text it could write
 from a number it could not. LANGUAGE.md:3913-3921, new prose since
 vox #40 (Discrepancy 6) closed the segfault by extending the same
 compile-time guard to variables and, it turns out, to `value` too.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox docs/ledger/probes/files/FIL-103.vox -o p
 compile failed:
   error: Cannot write value anything to a file; a value's type is only
   known at runtime, and Write must know whether it holds text (which
   it writes) or a number (whose value it would use as an address).
   Copy it into a typed variable first - 'a text called plain is
   anything.' - and write that.
